  "title": "Seeing continues through saccades and blinks",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "de551a5c-376f-46cd-8ee4-e6498fbe5a33",
      "text": "Interruptions of stimulation by saccades and blinks do not interrupt seeing, as a missile still tracks a plane that briefly leaves its sights, because seeing consists in the exercise of mastery of the relevant contingencies, not in a continuous input.",
